      <h2>📍 Today's Watch List</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>PUC open meeting today, Nov. 5, 9:30 a.m.: ERCOT's presentations on the community impact RFI, Batch Zero verification and the Medium Load RFI; ERCOT's generic-docket proposal and Nov. 20 complaint deadline; the developers' request for oral argument; and whether Skybox gets added to the agenda.</li>
        <li>Riot: how fast the Corsicana substation expansion moves toward the first 400 MW in September 2027, and what KBW decides once its rating review ends.</li>
        <li>Hut 8 and Core Scientific earnings calls this week. KBW wants both to address timing risk on their signed Texas leases.</li>
        <li>Cipher's Reveille and CleanSpark's Sealy and Brazoria leases: whether either company signs before the session starts.</li>
        <li>Abbott: whether he keeps, changes or lifts the TCEQ permit pause before Hinojosa takes office Jan. 19.</li>
        <li>Hinojosa's first TCEQ and PUC appointments, and the data center bills filed for January's session.</li>
        <li>Comptroller-elect Eckhardt: what she says about the data center sales tax exemption her office will administer.</li>
        <li>ERCOT Medium Load RFI responses due at 5 p.m. Friday, Nov. 6, the same day as SB 6 large-load curtailment workshop #2. ERCOT also expects to finish its two remaining alternative dispute resolutions by Nov. 6.</li>
        <li>Batch Zero complaints stay paused until Nov. 10. ERCOT's second-round eligibility questions carry five-business-day deadlines.</li>
        <li>ERCOT will file its good-cause exception for loads that weren't energized by July 10 next week, for the PUC's Dec. 17 meeting.</li>
        <li>Bastrop: whether the council acted on the 48-turbine Cedar Creek gas plant.</li>
        <li>Core Scientific's TCEQ enforcement case in Denton, and Denton's moratorium vote, as early as Dec. 1.</li>
        <li>Docket 59399: ERCOT's conditions on the Comanche Peak–Amazon arrangement versus Vistra's commitment-based approach.</li>
        <li>Dallas: the Economic Development Committee's next meeting, when the deferred data center standards come back.</li>
        <li>ERCOT: Planning Working Group Nov. 9, Batch/CTP workshops Nov. 17 and 19, TAC Nov. 18, Large Load Working Group and a PUC open meeting Nov. 19, another PUC meeting Dec. 3.</li>
        <li>Comments on the draft large-load interconnection agreement are due Dec. 14. Chevron's final investment decision on its West Texas Microsoft project is due by the end of 2026.</li>
        <li>ERCOT's final community impact report and audit reports are due Dec. 10, and Abbott's permit pause is tied to the audit. The PUC meets Dec. 17.</li>
      </ul>

